Z||000000||Philphine||10-31-2001||02:59 PM||||if you were going with a changer would you consider getting a cassette head unit to save cost. consider that i don't have cassettes anymore, but don't need high power (sep. amps) or x-overs or any other built in tricks. i just need a radio and something to control the changer. stock radio with an fm modulator is not a option. i can get a cassette head for 1/2 of what the cd head cost. also it might be a theft deterent if someone looked in the dash and just saw a cassette head. waddaya think?<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||10-31-2001||03:04 PM||||That's how I'm set up.  A Sony tape-deck head unit connected to a Sony 10-disc changer behind the passenger seat. Works perfectly, and I'm pretty sure I'd do the same again.  Of course, it's the <B>only</B> tape deck I still own- and like you, I've got only CDs.||||reg||1
